    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe daily-limit rule for `POST /api/owners`, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (no `@RestController`):\n\n1. **`CheckOwnerDailyLimit`** (new function) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today via `OwnerRepository.findAll()`, and throws `OwnerDailyLimitException` once the count is \u2265 100. The new owner is still unsaved so it isn't counted. Mirrors the existing `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` step.\n\n2. **`OwnerDailyLimitException`** (checked exception) \u2014 carries the date and count.\n\n3. **`OwnerDailyLimitExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds **429 Too Many Requests** with `{\"errors\":[\"registrationDate\"]}`, matching the shape of the city-capacity handler.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** `...OwnerDailyLimitException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `checkDailyLimit` step (under `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `checkCityCapacity` and `build`.\n\nThe new owner defaults to `registrationDate = LocalDate.now()` in `BuildOwner`, so the test's 100 created owners are all dated today and the 101st create is correctly rejected with 429.",
