    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a faithful, additive mirror of the existing `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` triad, and matches this codebase's established conventions precisely:\n\n- **Logic is in the right unit.** A dedicated `CheckOwnerDailyLimit` function class sits alongside the sibling `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique` / `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique` / `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` guards, wired as its own pipeline step between `checkCityCapacity` and `build` \u2014 exactly where a new pre-build rejection belongs.\n- **Idiomatic method and naming.** `public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)`, the `static final MAX_...` constant, the `findAll()` loop-and-count, and the `throws` checked exception all follow `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` to the letter. Single public method per class, as AGENTS.md requires.\n- **Exception/handler pair matches convention.** `OwnerDailyLimitException(date, count)` mirrors `OwnerCityCapacityException(city, count)`, and the 429 handler reuses the same `ResponseEntity<Map<String,Object>>` + `errors` array shape as the 409 handler, naming `registrationDate`.\n- **Escalation YAML and `govern: [ transaction ]`** follow the existing files.\n\nThe `findAll()`-then-count-in-Java approach is duplicated between the two Check classes, but the predicates differ (city match vs. date match) and the codebase clearly favors one self-contained class per guard \u2014 extracting a shared helper would fight the established idiom rather than improve it. A maintainer of this repo would find this change entirely natural. (Efficiency of `findAll()` and off-by-one/timezone correctness are out of scope per the review instructions.)",
